From: pencilbsp <pencil.bsp@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: do not require host-cached state buffers

PanVK exposes host-visible coherent memory for the small damage and chroma
state buffers but does not set HOST_CACHED. Cached access is a performance
hint, not a correctness requirement, and demanding it stops the VA-API view
creator from being constructed at all on Mali-G610 -- the encoder is then
never used and the session silently falls back to encoding on the CPU.

Ask for host-visible and coherent, which is what the buffers actually need.
---
--- a/src/grd-rdp-view-creator-avc.c
+++ b/src/grd-rdp-view-creator-avc.c
@@ -724,8 +724,7 @@
                                   VK_BUFFER_USAGE_STORAGE_BUFFER_BIT;
   buffer_descriptor.size = view_creator_avc->state_buffer_size;
   buffer_descriptor.memory_flags = VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_VISIBLE_BIT |
-                                   VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_COHERENT_BIT |
-                                   VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_CACHED_BIT;
+                                   VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_COHERENT_BIT;
 
   *state_buffer_host = grd_vk_buffer_new (view_creator_avc->device,
                                           &buffer_descriptor,
